# ============================================================================
# EVAL SHEET: "Multi-objects" — intersecting objects test
# ============================================================================
# Requirement (verbatim): "Place several intersecting objects in the scene,
# such as, for example a sphere and a cylinder, and display the rendered
# image. Both objects should be visible and displayed without glitching,
# especially where both objects intersect."
# The key risk here is z-fighting / incorrect nearest-hit selection right
# at the intersection seam — that's where a broken hit_scene() (picking the
# wrong closest t, or not comparing across object types correctly) shows up.

#ambient strength/ratio RGB_col( , , )
A 0.2 255,255,255

#camera pos( , , ) camera_dir( , , ) field_of_view(in deg)
# Pulled back and slightly up so the intersection seam between the two
# shapes is clearly on-screen rather than hidden behind either object.
C 2,2,-12 -0.15,-0.1,1 70

#L pos( , , ) brightness_ratio RGB_col( , , )
L -5,6,-6 0.8 255,255,255

#sp sphere_center( , , ) diameter RGB_colour( , , )
sp 0,0,0 4 255,0,0

#cy center( , , ) axis_vector( , , ) diameter height RGB_colour( , , )
# Centred at x=1 (inside the sphere's radius-2 volume) so the cylinder's
# body visibly punches through the sphere rather than merely touching it.
cy 1,0,0 0,1,0 1.5 6 0,255,150
